{"name":"Lady’s Cushions Pink","hex":"#c99bb0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lady","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The mistress of a household.","A woman of breeding or higher class, a woman of authority."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To address as “lady”."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lady"},{"term":"cushions","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of cushion"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of cushion"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cushions"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cushion","blocks":[{"text":"A cushion is a soft bag of some ornamental material, usually stuffed with wool, hair, feathers, polyester staple fiber, non-woven material, cotton, or even paper torn into fragments. It may be used for sitting or kneeling upon, or to soften the hardness or angularity of a chair or couch. Decorative cushions often have a patterned cover material, and are used as decoration for furniture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Throw_Pillows_%28Scatter_Cushions%29.jpg/330px-Throw_Pillows_%28Scatter_Cushions%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cushion","wikidata":"Q10971235"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"},{"title":"Lady","blocks":[{"text":"A lady is a woman who behaves in a polite way. Once used to describe only women of a high social class or status, the female counterpart of lord, now it may refer to any adult woman, as gentleman can be used for men."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady","wikidata":"Q1378024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%98%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%83%D0%BA_%D0%BC%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B5%D1%98_%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5_%D1%98%D1%83%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5.jpg/500px-%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%98%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%83%D0%BA_%D0%BC%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B5%D1%98_%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5_%D1%98%D1%83%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%98%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%83%D0%BA_%D0%BC%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B5%D1%98_%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5_%D1%98%D1%83%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5.jpg/1280px-%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%98%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%83%D0%BA_%D0%BC%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B5%D1%98_%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5_%D1%98%D1%83%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%98%D0%B5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%98%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%83%D0%BA_%D0%BC%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B5%D1%98_%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%98%